# Exercises Fulfillment & Shipping against the compose stack (`make up`): Staff read the Warehouses,
# Checkout asks for Shipping quotes, a Shipment goes from creation through pick and pack to
# delivery by the mock carrier's webhooks, a replacement is made for an RMA on its Order, and a
# Customer reads a Warehouse's return address. Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP
# client; the token requests store tokens for the ones after them.
# Checkout's and Orchestration's client secrets and the carrier webhook secret are the stack's own:
# run it in the `dev` environment, whose http-client.private.env.json holds them (the root README's
# "Secrets" says how to write it).

@fulfillment = http://localhost:8099
@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Checkout's own token (client credentials)
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=checkout&client_secret={{checkoutClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("checkoutToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The Warehouses, through the gateway as the Admin Console would: Berlin, the default, and Amsterdam
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A German address, as Checkout: from WH-BER at domestic prices, STANDARD €4.99 and EXPRESS €9.99
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"recipientName": "Erika Mustermann", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "10115",
                 "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE"},
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### A Dutch address: from WH-AMS, at domestic prices
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"recipientName": "Jan Jansen", "line1": "Damrak 1", "postcode": "1012 LG",
                 "city": "Amsterdam", "country": "NL"},
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### A French address: no Warehouse in France, so from the default WH-BER at EU prices, €9.99 and €19.99
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"recipientName": "Marie Dupont", "line1": "1 rue de Rivoli", "postcode": "75001",
                 "city": "Paris", "country": "FR"},
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### Outside the EU: 422, reason shippingUnavailable
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"country": "US"}, "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### A Currency the mock carrier has no table for: 422, reason shippingUnavailable
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"country": "DE"}, "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "USD"}

### A malformed country: 400 naming destination.country
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"country": "Germany"}, "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### As Staff: 403, only Checkout quotes
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"country": "DE"}, "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### Through the gateway: 404, quotes are internal
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipping/quotes
Authorization: Bearer {{checkoutToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"destination": {"country": "DE"}, "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "currency": "EUR"}

### Orchestration's own token (client credentials), for the fulfillment Saga's commands
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=orchestration&client_secret={{orchestrationClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("orchestrationToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Shipments. As the fulfillment Saga: create a Shipment for a new Order of the demo phone, to Germany.
### 201, AWAITING_PICK from WH-BER, the line named and IMEI-tracked from Catalog's Product
< {%
  request.variables.set("orderId", $random.uuid);
%}
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "customerId": "http-demo-customer",
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "shippingAddress": {"recipientName": "Erika Mustermann", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "10115",
                     "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE"},
 "shippingOption": {"id": "EXPRESS", "carrier": "Mock Carrier", "cost": {"amountMinor": 999, "currency": "EUR"},
                    "estimatedDays": 1}}

> {%
  client.global.set("shipmentId", response.body.id);
  client.global.set("shipmentOrderId", response.body.orderId);
%}

### A second Shipment for the same Order: 409, reason shipmentExists
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{shipmentOrderId}}", "customerId": "http-demo-customer",
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "shippingAddress": {"recipientName": "Erika Mustermann", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "10115",
                     "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE"},
 "shippingOption": {"id": "EXPRESS", "carrier": "Mock Carrier", "cost": {"amountMinor": 999, "currency": "EUR"}}}

### Through the gateway: 404, only the fulfillment Saga creates Shipments
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Staff's fulfillment queue under Berlin, through the gateway: awaiting pick, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?status=AWAITING_PICK&warehouseId=WH-BER
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Packing before picking: 409, reason illegalTransition
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serialNumbers": {"PHN-PIXEL-9": ["490154203237518"]}}

### Staff pick it: PICKED, by the Staff user
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/pick
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### An IMEI whose check digit is wrong: 422 naming serialNumbers.PHN-PIXEL-9[0]
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serialNumbers": {"PHN-PIXEL-9": ["490154203237517"]}}

### A valid IMEI, new on every run: PACKED, with the IMEI on its line
< {%
  const body = Array.from({length: 14}, () => Math.floor(Math.random() * 10)).join("");
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {
    let d = Number(body[13 - i]);
    if (i % 2 === 0) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) d -= 9; }
    sum += d;
  }
  request.variables.set("imei", body + ((10 - sum % 10) % 10));
%}
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serialNumbers": {"PHN-PIXEL-9": ["{{imei}}"]}}

### As the fulfillment Saga: dispatch it. SHIPPED, with the mock carrier's tracking number; its Carrier
### webhooks follow 10, 20 and 30 seconds later
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/dispatch
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}

> {% client.global.set("trackingNumber", response.body.trackingNumber); %}

### Half a minute later: DELIVERED, with three Tracking events, deliveredAt, and CARRIER in its history
GET {{fulfillment}}/shipments/{{shipmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### A Carrier webhook, signed as the mock signs it with the stack's carrier secret, through the gateway
### without a token, delivered twice: 200 both times, recorded once, and the status stays DELIVERED
< {%
  const body = JSON.stringify({eventId: "trk-http-" + $random.uuid, trackingNumber: client.global.get("trackingNumber"), status: "IN_TRANSIT", occurredAt: new Date().toISOString()});
  request.variables.set("carrierBody", body);
  request.variables.set("carrierSignature", "sha256=" + crypto.hmac.sha256().withTextSecret(request.environment.get("carrierWebhookSecret")).updateWithText(body).digest().toHex());
%}
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/webhooks/carrier
Carrier-Signature: {{carrierSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{carrierBody}}

### A Carrier webhook with a wrong signature: 401
POST {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/webhooks/carrier
Carrier-Signature: sha256=00
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": "trk-forged", "trackingNumber": "{{trackingNumber}}", "status": "DELIVERED",
 "occurredAt": "2026-10-13T10:00:00Z"}

### Holding a delivered Shipment: 409, reason illegalTransition
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/hold
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "authorization_expired"}

### The Order's Shipment as Staff read it by Order
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?orderId={{shipmentOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Replacements. As the returns Saga: a replacement phone for an RMA on that Order, to the Order Shipment's
### address. 201, kind REPLACEMENT naming the RMA, AWAITING_PICK from WH-BER
< {%
  request.variables.set("rmaId", $random.uuid);
%}
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind": "REPLACEMENT", "rmaId": "{{rmaId}}", "orderId": "{{shipmentOrderId}}", "customerId": "http-demo-customer",
 "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "shippingAddress": {"recipientName": "Erika Mustermann", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "10115",
                     "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE"},
 "shippingOption": {"id": "EXPRESS", "carrier": "Mock Carrier", "cost": {"amountMinor": 999, "currency": "EUR"},
                    "estimatedDays": 1}}

> {%
  client.global.set("replacementId", response.body.id);
  client.global.set("replacementRmaId", response.body.rmaId);
%}

### A second replacement for the same RMA: 409, reason shipmentExists, with the first in shipment
POST {{fulfillment}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"kind": "REPLACEMENT", "rmaId": "{{replacementRmaId}}", "orderId": "{{shipmentOrderId}}",
 "customerId": "http-demo-customer", "lines": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}],
 "shippingAddress": {"recipientName": "Erika Mustermann", "line1": "Hauptstraße 5", "postcode": "10115",
                     "city": "Berlin", "country": "DE"},
 "shippingOption": {"id": "EXPRESS", "carrier": "Mock Carrier", "cost": {"amountMinor": 999, "currency": "EUR"}}}

### The Order's own Shipment is still what its Order reads: kind ORDER
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?orderId={{shipmentOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The RMA's replacement, as Staff read it by RMA
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?rmaId={{replacementRmaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Staff's queue of replacements awaiting pick, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?status=AWAITING_PICK&kind=REPLACEMENT
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### The demo Customer's token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### A Warehouse's name and return address, as any signed-in Customer reads it, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/warehouses/WH-AMS
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Warehouse that isn't configured: 404
GET {{gateway}}/api/fulfillment-shipping/warehouses/WH-XXX
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
